WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.490
- [Narrator] Finland is
now officially a member

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.814
of the world's largest military alliance.

00:00:04.814 --> 00:00:07.350
(people clapping)

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.200
- This is an historic day.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.610
We welcome Finland as a
newest member of our alliance.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.320
- [Narrator] The Nordic
nation completed one

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.340
of the fastest accession
processes in NATO's history.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.670
Finland applied to join in
response to Russia's invasion

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.940
of Ukraine in February 2022.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:27.840
In the process,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.240
Finland ended its decades-old policy

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.220
of military non-alignment.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.500
- It will change Russia's
posture towards Europe

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.240
and NATO in general in the future.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.490
- [Narrator] Here's what
the historic expansion means

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.283
for the alliance and security in Europe.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.020
First of all, Finland
adds more than 800 miles

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.003
to NATO's border with Russia.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.600
It also extends the area in which NATO

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.370
can conduct its operations.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.600
The territory spans

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.110
about 1,000 miles from the
Baltic Sea to the Arctic.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.790
- Finland joining NATO also means

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:03.810
that the NATO alliance comes
closer to the Kola Peninsula,

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.330
which has great strategic
importance for Russia.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.690
It's where many of its nuclear
capabilities are based.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.150
- [Narrator] And Finland
doesn't come empty handed

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.220
as it's one of Europe's best defended

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.800
and best armed countries.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.620
- Finland has maintained a posture

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.870
against Russia where it
was ready for a conflict.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.780
It can mobilize over 800,000 troops

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.660
and it's also continued
to modernize its military.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:28.493
In the past decade,

00:01:28.493 --> 00:01:33.090
it's received surface to
air missiles, rocket systems

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:36.810
and it's even received
the F-35s from the US.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:37.980
- The Kremlin's decision

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.670
to invade Ukraine radically
changed Finnish public opinion

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:44.400
on the country's non-aligned
defense doctrine.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.400
In May 2022, support for
NATO membership lept to 76%,

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.630
a fundamental shift from
30% in January that year

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:56.310
just before the invasion.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.920
And for Russian president Vladimir Putin,

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.160
Finland's accession is a
major strategic setback.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.120
- There is definitely a sort

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:06.930
of a paradox in this, in
these developments, given

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.500
that we know that Vladimir
Putin wants to divide NATO

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.400
and the Western alliance.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.020
But what he's actually facing now

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.560
is a more united Western front than ever.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.883
- President Putin wanted
to slam NATO's door shut.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:25.590
Today we show the world that he failed.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.320
- [Narrator] Russia said
NATO's enlargement is a threat

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.505
to its security and national interests.

00:02:31.505 --> 00:02:35.255
(Sergei speaking in Russian)

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.740
- [Narrator] Finland's
membership of NATO came

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.070
after months of diplomatic
disputes with Turkey.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.930
Finland applied to join the Alliance

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.990
at the same time as
Sweden, but Turkey alleged

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.900
the two Northern European
countries had connections

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.380
to Kurdish militant groups
fighting the Turkish state.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.590
Eventually, Ankara ratified
Finland's membership

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.560
but Sweden is still waiting
to join the Alliance,

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.170
which needs the approval
of all existing members

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.390
to accept any new entrants.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.880
- Sweden definitely hopes to be a member

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.440
of NATO by the end of the year.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.120
- Our persistent efforts

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:16.044
for a rapid Swedish
membership will continue.

00:03:16.044 --> 00:03:18.794
(dramatic music)

